  "preamble": "Depalatalization (hardening) of the palatalized bilabial nasal [mʲ] to plain [m]. Palatalized labials are perceptually weak word-finally, and several Slavic languages hardened them there: Old East Slavic семь (13th c. /ˈsʲɛːmʲ/) 'seven' keeps its soft labial in standard Russian [sʲemʲ] but has hard [m] in Ukrainian сім [sʲim] and Belarusian сем [sʲem].",
  "phoneticEffects": "Depalatalization, Hardening, Word-Final Position",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Ukrainian",
      "languageFamily": "East Slavic",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Old East Slavic семь /ˈsʲɛːmʲ/ (13th c.) 'seven'",
          "to": "сім [sʲim]",
          "note": "The final soft labial hardened, as in other Ukrainian final labials (голуб 'pigeon' against Russian голубь)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "language": "Belarusian",
      "languageFamily": "East Slavic",
